# Shared by both packages, which is why their format scripts pass
# `--ignore-path ../.prettierignore` explicitly.
#
# Prettier resolves a config file by walking up from each file it formats, but
# it looks for the ignore file in the working directory only. Since the format
# scripts run from backend/ and frontend/, this file would otherwise be found
# by neither, and `format:check` would fail on built output -- which is how
# that was caught.
#
# Generated or vendored output. Reformatting any of it produces a large diff
# that nobody authored and that the next tool run reverts.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# npm owns the formatting of these; `prettier --write` reflows them and the
# next `npm install` puts them back.
package-lock.json

# Screenshot artefacts from scripts/a11y-browser-check.mjs
frontend/a11y-shots/

# Local data
data/
*.db
